    "note": "All sequences are shown from 5′ to 3′. RT denotes reverse transcription. Primers cover seven receptor chains: four TCR chains and immunoglobulin heavy, κ and λ chains. Heavy-chain primers target five isotypes: IgA, IgD, IgE, IgG and IgM. Two PCR primers were used for IgG. IUPAC degenerate bases are M = A/C, K = G/T, S = G/C, W = A/T, Y = C/T and R = A/G. The table contains 23 primers: 11 RT and 12 PCR primers."
